      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Start recovery immediately on the Google Account Recovery Page.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Start recovery immediately on the Google Account Recovery Page"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Google does not offer live phone or chat support for account recovery. You must use their automated tools.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          6,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 1: Get Back Into Your Account"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Go to the link: Open a browser and visit Google Account Recovery.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Enter your email: Type in your hacked Gmail address and click Next.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Try another way: If the hacker changed your password, click \"Try another way\" when prompted.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Use a familiar device: Use a phone, tablet, or computer you used to sign in before, and stay in a usual location like home or work. Google checks these details to verify you.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Answer prompts: Follow the on-screen questions as best as you can. Provide an alternate contact email or phone number where Google can reach you."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step 2: Secure Your Account After Sign-In"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Once you regain access, take these steps right away:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Change your password: Pick a strong, unique password that you do not use on any other website.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check email forwarding: Go to Gmail Settings (gear icon) > See all settings > Forwarding and POP/IMAP. Make sure the hacker did not set up automatic forwarding to an unknown address.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              10
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Remove unknown devices: Go to your Google Account Security Page, look under Your devices, and sign out any devices or sessions you do not recognize.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Google Account Security Page",
                "link": "https://myaccount.google.com/security"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Update recovery info: Verify that your own recovery phone number and recovery email are listed.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              11
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Turn on 2-Step Verification: Add an extra layer of security using a phone prompt or passkey."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Note: Be careful of online scams. Most users on Google Account Help Forum agree that standard recovery can be very difficult if recovery options were changed. Google never charges money and never provides phone support for recovery.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Google Account Help Forum",
            "link": "https://support.google.com/accounts/thread/196112130/account-hacked-fully-locked-out-how-to-recover?hl=en"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
